# Queue row 259. This is the exact reduction a PR #51 reviewer shipped by hand,
# and all 7 tests of the day stayed green under it: the only bounded-excerpt
# test planted its marker at the END of the synthetic stream, so a tail-only
# excerpt still contained it. The head half is the half that says WHAT BROKE -
# the first failing test and its assertion - while the tail is the TAP summary
# that says how much. Losing the head silently is a diagnosability regression
# that would ship.
#
# The suite header is TARGETED at the one test that owns this behaviour rather
# than the whole file, because the file's other bounded-excerpt tests pass under
# the tail-only reduction and would dilute the evidence. A targeted header is
# accepted only on a pair of counts - >= 1 test run and green on the clean tree,
# the SAME count with >= 1 failure under the mutant - never on an exit code:
# `-m unittest -k <typo>` runs 0 tests and exits 0, which reads as a pass.
# Verified: clean 1 test / OK, mutant 1 test / 1 failure.
# Body generated per tests/CONTRACT.md rule 4.
